{"task":"transcribe","language":"english","duration":49.869998931884766,"text":"The Tower of the Winds is an eight-sided marble tower built about 2,000 years ago by an astronomer called Andronikos. Each of its eight sides faces one direction, and on every side, a wind is carved as a flying man. The north wind holds a shell to blow through. The west wind scatters flowers from the fold of his cloak. Under each carving, there was a sundial. So far, there is nothing magic about it. If the sun is out, a shadow tells you the time. The clever part is what happened when clouds came over. Inside the tower, a water clock ran, fed by a spring on the Acropolis. Water dripped at a steady rate and counted the hours through rain and through the night. On the roof, a bronze weather vane turned, so you also knew which wind was blowing.","words":[{"word":"The","start":0,"end":0.5199999809265137},{"word":"Tower","start":0.5199999809265137,"end":0.8999999761581421},{"word":"of","start":0.8999999761581421,"end":1.159999966621399},{"word":"the","start":1.159999966621399,"end":1.5},{"word":"Winds","start":1.5,"end":1.5},{"word":"is","start":1.5,"end":1.9199999570846558},{"word":"an","start":1.9199999570846558,"end":2.240000009536743},{"word":"eight","start":2.240000009536743,"end":2.5799999237060547},{"word":"sided","start":2.5799999237060547,"end":2.9200000762939453},{"word":"marble","start":2.9200000762939453,"end":3.4200000762939453},{"word":"tower","start":3.4200000762939453,"end":3.8399999141693115},{"word":"built","start":3.8399999141693115,"end":4.380000114440918},{"word":"about","start":4.380000114440918,"end":4.78000020980835},{"word":"2","start":4.78000020980835,"end":5.420000076293945},{"word":"000","start":5.420000076293945,"end":5.5},{"word":"years","start":5.5,"end":5.880000114440918},{"word":"ago","start":5.880000114440918,"end":6.139999866485596},{"word":"by","start":6.139999866485596,"end":6.380000114440918},{"word":"an","start":6.380000114440918,"end":6.679999828338623},